    "title": "A Marine Father, an Air Force Son, and the Distance Between Them - NewsBreak",
    "text": "17 hours ago My father has been running longer than I've been alive. As his son, without understanding or explanation, he expected me to run with him. He was a Marine, but he'd been running long before he enlisted. He escaped from an abusive, alcoholic home in North Carolina at age 16. He eventually found safety and structure at Camp Pendleton. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak",
